===Etymology 3===
From {{inh|en|enm|mirken}}, probably from {{der|en|non|myrkja}}, {{m|non|myrkva|t=to make dark, darken}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*mirkwijaną}}, {{m|gem-pro|*mirkwajaną|t=to make dark}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*mergʷ-|t=to flicker; to darken; to be dark}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# To make [[murky]] or be murky; to [[cloud]] or [[obscure]], or to be [[clouded]] or [[obscured]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1918|author=Booth Tarkington|title=The Magnificent Ambersons|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140811201712/http://etext.virginia.edu/etcbin/ot2www-pubeng?specfile=%2Ftexts%2Fenglish%2Fmodeng%2Fpublicsearch%2Fmodengpub.o2w
|passage=Dawn had been '''murking''' through the smoky windows, growing stronger for half an hour...}}

